# Wholesale Customer Spending Analysis

## Project Overview

This project explores the spending patterns of wholesale customers across six product categories: Fresh, Milk, Grocery, Frozen, Detergents_Paper, and Delicassen.

The analysis aims to understand how customer spending varies across product categories, examine differences between customer channels and regions, and identify unusual spending patterns that may influence statistical summaries.

Using Python and exploratory data analysis techniques, the project investigates data quality, descriptive statistics, distributions, relative variability, and potential outliers. The goal is to develop a clearer understanding of wholesale customer purchasing behaviour and demonstrate a structured, evidence-based approach to data analysis.## Dataset Description

The dataset contains 440 observations and 8 columns, with each observation representing a wholesale customer.

It includes two categorical variables, `Channel` and `Region`, and six numerical variables representing annual spending across different product categories.

### Variables

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `Channel` | Customer channel: Horeca or Retail |
| `Region` | Geographical region associated with the customer |
| `Fresh` | Annual spending on fresh products |
| `Milk` | Annual spending on milk products |
| `Grocery` | Annual spending on grocery products |
| `Frozen` | Annual spending on frozen products |
| `Detergents_Paper` | Annual spending on detergents and paper products |
| `Delicassen` | Annual spending on delicatessen products |
